[38,'What is the best source for validating whether a discovered dependency is functionally required?','Application-owner knowledge combined with technical discovery evidence','A random user survey','The browser cache','An unrelated service map','서비스 담당자의 아키텍처 지식과 실제 연결·Pattern 증거를 함께 검증합니다.'],
[39,'A service map changes on every run. Which issue should be investigated?','Unstable identifiers, transient connections, or inconsistent discovery access','The page title length','The number of exam questions','The footer copyright year','식별값과 접근 권한, 일시적 연결이 매번 달라지는지 확인해 반복 가능한 결과를 확보합니다.'],
[40,'Which metric most directly measures mapping completeness?','The percentage of expected service components and dependencies represented','The number of portal visits','The number of active users','The count of email templates','예상 아키텍처와 비교해 필요한 CI와 관계가 맵에 얼마나 포함됐는지 측정합니다.'],
[41,'Which metric is useful for map correctness?','The rate of validated CIs and relationships that truly belong to the service','The number of browser tabs','The count of password resets','The length of a service name','실제 서비스에 속하는 것으로 검증된 CI·관계 비율은 정확성 판단에 유용합니다.'],
[42,'What should be documented for each production application service?','Owner, purpose, entry points, expected topology, credentials dependency, and validation criteria','Only its display color','Only the creator name','Only the latest incident number','운영 가능한 맵을 위해 소유권, 진입점, 예상 구조, 접근 전제와 검증 기준을 기록합니다.'],
[43,'What is the benefit of scheduling regular rediscovery?','Keep the map aligned with infrastructure and application changes','Prevent all infrastructure changes','Replace change management','Guarantee zero alerts','정기 재탐색은 실제 환경 변화가 서비스 맵과 CMDB에 반영되도록 합니다.'],
[44,'What should happen when planned architecture changes introduce a new tier?','Update mapping logic if needed, rediscover, and validate the new dependency','Manually close every discovery status','Remove the service owner','Disable the application permanently','새 계층을 탐색할 수 있도록 Pattern·접근 전제를 확인하고 재탐색 후 검증합니다.'],
[45,'Why coordinate Service Mapping with change management?','Map changes can validate implementation and improve impact assessment','Changes automatically create credentials','It removes the need for CMDB','It prevents all outages','정확한 맵은 변경 영향 평가를 돕고 변경 후 실제 토폴로지를 검증하는 자료가 됩니다.'],
[46,'An entry point resolves to multiple IP addresses. What should the implementer verify?','All relevant targets and load-balancing behavior are correctly represented','The portal has one homepage','The exam configuration uses one duration','The application has one user','DNS·로드밸런싱으로 여러 대상이 존재하면 각 대상과 관계가 서비스 구조에 맞게 탐색되는지 확인합니다.'],
[47,'What is the role of credentials in top-down mapping?','Allow authorized access needed to identify applications and follow connections','Determine service-map colors','Create CI classes automatically','Set incident SLAs','Credential은 호스트·애플리케이션에 필요한 최소 권한 접근을 제공해 데이터 수집을 가능하게 합니다.'],
[48,'Which credential practice is recommended?','Use least privilege with clear ownership and rotation','Share an unrestricted personal account','Embed passwords in pattern scripts','Disable credential testing','최소 권한, 소유자, 안전한 보관과 회전 정책을 갖춘 서비스 계정을 사용합니다.'],
[49,'A MID Server can reach a host but authentication fails. Which evidence is most useful?','Credential test results and discovery-phase logs','Portal analytics','Survey responses','Report colors','Credential Test와 Discovery 단계 로그로 선택된 Credential과 인증 오류를 확인합니다.'],
[50,'What should be considered when placing MID Servers for Service Mapping?','Network reachability, security zones, capacity, and resilience','Only browser resolution','Only the service name','Only exam location','네트워크 구간·방화벽·용량·고가용성을 고려해 대상에 안정적으로 접근하도록 배치합니다.'],
[51,'How should multiple MID Servers be used for a large environment?','Distribute workloads and provide suitable capabilities or clustering where needed','Run every job on one personal laptop','Give each one a different CMDB','Disable scheduling','용량과 네트워크 범위에 맞춰 작업을 분산하고 필요한 Capability와 복원력을 구성합니다.'],
[52,'What does a stale mapped CI most likely indicate?','Rediscovery, data-source precedence, or lifecycle handling needs review','The font is unsupported','The exam expired','The entry point is a user record','실제 환경과 불일치하면 재탐색 성공 여부와 데이터 소스 우선순위, CI 수명주기를 확인합니다.'],
[53,'Why is a service owner important during implementation?','They confirm service boundaries, expected dependencies, and acceptable results','They run every MID Server command','They replace all technical SMEs','They control CMDB encryption keys','서비스 소유자는 비즈니스 범위와 기대 결과를 승인하고 기술 담당자와 누락·오탐을 검증합니다.'],
[54,'Which approach is best for onboarding many services?','Use a repeatable intake, readiness, mapping, validation, and handoff process','Map all services without owners','Skip credential planning','Accept every discovered connection','표준 Intake와 준비도 확인, 구현, 검증, 운영 인계 절차로 품질을 일관되게 유지합니다.'],
[55,'What is an appropriate readiness prerequisite for a mapping engagement?','Known service scope, SMEs, network access, credentials, and a healthy CMDB foundation','A custom portal theme','A completed employee survey','An empty incident table','범위·담당자·접근·Credential·CMDB 기반이 준비되어야 시행착오를 줄일 수 있습니다.'],
[56,'Which symptom suggests a firewall or network-path problem?','The MID Server cannot establish the required connection to a target port','A map has a long name','An owner has two groups','A report has no chart','필요 포트로 연결 자체가 되지 않으면 방화벽, 라우팅, 대상 서비스 상태를 점검합니다.'],
[57,'Which symptom more strongly suggests a parsing problem?','The command returns data but expected variables remain empty','The target port is unreachable','The MID Server is down','DNS returns no address','명령 결과는 있지만 변수가 비어 있으면 반환 형식과 Parse 작업을 확인합니다.'],
[58,'What is the best response to a missing downstream database on the map?','Trace the connection step, returned endpoint, credentials, classification, and identification results','Add an unrelated database manually','Delete the application service','Disable reconciliation','연결 단계부터 반환 Endpoint, 접근, 분류와 식별을 순서대로 추적해 근본 원인을 찾습니다.'],
[59,'Why avoid permanent manual relationships when automated discovery should own them?','They can become stale and hide mapping defects','They prevent all incidents','They consume user licenses','They change exam duration','수동 관계는 실제 변화와 동기화되지 않고 자동 탐색 결함을 가릴 수 있습니다.'],
[60,'What marks a successful Service Mapping handoff to operations?','Documented ownership, validated map, monitored schedules, troubleshooting procedure, and quality KPIs','A single successful browser load','No service owner','Disabled rediscovery','소유권과 검증된 결과, 스케줄 감시, 장애 대응 절차와 품질 지표가 운영에 인계되어야 합니다.']
